	(text "Power: the XT connectors sit on the root sheet. Each input: 1 A time-lag fuse, then a TVS to GND (D-45).\nThe TVS clamps transients and conducts on reverse polarity, so the fuse opens. D6 limits Q1 VGS to 15 V.\n+12V_RLY: 12 V +-5 % (RT1 coil range 10.2 to 13.2 V). +12V_SW: +12V_RLY switched by Q1 when RLY_EN is high.\nRLY_EN is active-high with R3 pull-down: no signal = relays off (D-39). C2 not fitted (soft start option).\nClamp nets: each coil diode goes to CLAMP_SW (rows, K1) or CLAMP_RLY (K0). Zeners D2 // D4 and D3 // D5 (24 V) return\nthe coil energy to the rail: drain peak about 37.5 V. Two in parallel: one open zener does not remove the clamp.\n+3V3: U1 LP2985-33 from +5V, for the expanders and the I2C bus. R4 0R: lift to measure the 3.3 V load (D-120).\nBulk C6, C7 47 uF polymer at the 12 V entries (D-129). Test points TP1 to TP5 on every rail; the fuses F1 to F3\nserve as the current links of the input rails (D-120).\nMounting holes not grounded; H1 is the only bond (JP1 open, C1 not fitted). The case bonds to the RVS earth bar at one point only.\nSupports S1 to S6: plated, at case potential through the standoffs; each on its own net CHASSIS_Sn, joined to nothing
else on the board. C8 to C13 are local bond options to GND, not fitted (D-132, D-162)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
